==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{uder|en|fr|cocon}}, diminutive of {{m|fr|coque||shell}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/kəˈkuːn/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-cocoon.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{homophones|en|kokoon}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# The [[silk]]y [[protective]] [[case]] spun by the [[larva|larvae]] of some [[insect]]s in which they [[metamorphose]], the [[pupa]].
# Any similar protective case, whether real or metaphorical.

====Derived terms====
{{der2|en|brood cocoon|jet cocoon}}

